(text "Sheet 3: SC95F8523 controller, supplies and connectors. Pin numbers: SOP28/TSSOP28 (SinOne datasheet V0.3)." (at 25.4 30.48 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0)) (justify left top)) (uuid ac681182-934b-548b-819a-0265d5e95730))
(text "Gate-drive supply VDRV = battery (11.2-14.6 V) through R47/C49.\nIR2104 needs 10-20 V on VCC (UVLO about 8-9.8 V), so no regulator." (at 172.72 40.64 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid a6ddaf67-f060-58f5-aa2e-9faab617b979))
(text "5 V logic rail, always on. L78L05: about 3-6 mA quiescent, +/-5 %.\nADC uses the internal 2.048 V reference; fault thresholds use U10 (sheet 4)." (at 172.72 116.84 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid 88c3420c-5d2c-5bf5-b72d-8bbe0ed4d98b))
(text "NTC inputs: 100k pull-up, 10k B3950 NTC (off-board),\n12-bit ADC with 2.048 V reference." (at 320.04 137.16 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid dc7879cd-babb-5a4d-b558-36b29cb49df4))
(text "Notes\n- Unused pins P1.0, P1.6, P0.5, P0.6, P0.7 and PWM3: set as outputs driven low in firmware.\n- NTC readings scale with the 5 V rail: correct them with the internal 1/4 VDD ADC channel.\n- C25/C26: use the load capacitance from the crystal datasheet (typ. 10-15 pF).\n- Every ADC divider has 100 nF at the divider. Analog ground (dividers, NTCs, U5/U6) joins power ground at one point near R14.\n- J3: SinOne 2-wire programming (tCK/tDIO). J4: PIR / motion sensor. J5: service UART." (at 25.4 238.76 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid cf05d87a-a12b-57be-9a51-a461a175d8e3))
)
